[ ] Use restrict keyword wherever appropriate (only hb_tree and pr_tree use it).
[X] Fix skiplist prev pointers.
[ ] Implement iterator compare for the hash tables (iterator remove is done).
[ ] Reformat to 80 columns (~400 longer lines, e.g. the vtable thunk tables).
[ ] Optimize double-rotations.
[X] Fix bugs in weight balanced tree.
[ ] Optimize skiplist.

Features (new API, not bug fixes):
[ ] skiplist_select(), so dict_select() works on the skip list (O(n)).
[ ] A way to seed dict_rand(): random() is never seeded, so every process
    gets the same treap priorities and skip list levels. It also yields only
    31 bits, so skip list levels above 16 are never used.

Versioning:
[ ] DICT_VERSION_* in dict.h still say 0.3.0 while releases are 1.0.x; the
    macros are compiled into applications, so decide before changing them.
[ ] The GNUmakefile installs libdict.so.2 (INSTALL_LIBVER) while CMake builds
    soname libdict.so.1.0.

Candidates for the next major version (API/ABI breaking):
[ ] Rename itor_vtable's 'invalid' member to 'invalidate'.
[ ] Make dict_key_func and dict_icompare_func take/return const pointers.
[ ] Prefix BEGIN_DECL/END_DECL (LIBDICT_), keeping the old names as aliases.

Portability and limits:
[ ] Fallback for random(), which is POSIX only (e.g. MSVC).
[ ] hashtable2 iterators use an int slot index, wrong beyond 2^31 slots.
[ ] dict_prime_geq() returns a smaller value for n > 4294967291.

Build, tests and CI (propose before adding, see CLAUDE.md):
[ ] CI: Release next to Debug, an ASan + UBSan job, a LIBDICT_SLOW_TESTS=1
    job, QEMU jobs for arm64, armv7, i386 and s390x, and a clang make build.
[ ] Smoke tests for demo, anagram and benchmark in CTest.
